  "finalText": "I cancelled the wireless mouse line (L1) on O-2003, refunded it to Marcus's card, and put the two mice back in stock.\n\n- **Cancel:** L1 (P-MOU, qty 2) had not shipped, so this was a cancellation rather than a return. The cancel call on its own issued no refund and moved no stock.\n- **Refund:** I refunded 7,350 cents to the card (refund RF-1). That is what he actually paid for L1 after discount code MOUSE25. The list price would have been 9,800, which is more than he paid. There is no store credit, because the policy sends refunds for lines that never shipped back to the original payment method.\n- **Restock:** P-MOU stock went from 30 to 32, since stock had been set aside for the line.\n- **Untouched:** L2 (hub) and L3 (cables) are still pending, so they ship as planned. The shipping address is unchanged, and I didn't touch any other orders or products.\n\nI re-read O-2003 afterwards and it shows 7,350 refunded, L1 cancelled and L2 and L3 still pending. I didn't re-check the customer's store-credit balance, but I made no store-credit calls.\n\nThe current date is 2026-07-25 in the system, not the 2026-10-05 in my instructions. That doesn't change anything here, because the policy applies to a line that never shipped whatever the order's age.",
